#[doc = r#"Defines an OpVolume via a reference objects filter and buffers. Geometry, position and velocity of the referential object shall be treated identically as in the referenced object, but expanded per the defined buffers. Geometry shall progress through time as the referenced geometry progresses through time. Geometry shall be updated as the referenced geometry is updated. Only objects containing a geometry definition, and not be defined referentially, shall be used as a reference object. Only the current geometry of active reference objects shall be considered. Inactive geometry shall be ignored and future or past geometry shall be ignored. For the example of weather, this means that only the current state of weather will be used, rather than the full area across the full forecast summed up. An AND relationship can be created between multiple characteristics by including them in one filter type. An OR relationship can be created by putting characteristics in different filters."#]
